ClaudeReader changes (based on BDReader)
ClaudeReader 1.1 (31/10/2026)
	-Reader bar above the page: back to the library, comic title and position, reading mode (Panels, Page, Strip,
	 Scroll), right to left, pages side bar and fullscreen; hidden in fullscreen
	-Activity bar with the places only (Library, Store, Reader, Settings): Open in the File menu (Ctrl+O),
	 Help with F1, fullscreen also with F11
	-Scroll mode (W) for webtoons and manhwa: the pages one under the other at the same width, scrolled continuously
	 (wheel, arrows, Page Up/Down, Space, dragging), Ctrl+wheel or +/- for the width, only the pages around the view in memory
	-Settings: panel highlight style (frame, line, dim the rest, corners), thickness and color, with a preview
	-Settings > Stores: the installed stores; add a store from the catalog (stores/index.json of the repository,
	 with updates), from a .lua file or from a link (GitHub file pages work too); remove or restore a store.
	 The catalog address can be changed with the CLAUDEREADER_STORE_CATALOG environment variable (to test a catalog)
	-Store catalog: xkcd (every comic as a chapter)
	-Store scripts have a time limit (instructions) and a memory limit (256 MB): a store stuck in a loop gives an error
	 instead of freezing ClaudeReader (#3)
	-Bug fixed: the Delete button of the tags in Settings did nothing
	-Panels: the last page, and the pages of one or two page comics, are read panel by panel too; the cover (first
	 page of 3 or more) and a first or last page without panels are shown whole (#6)
	-Library: folders of images are comics, as the store downloads in Images format (#5); comics up to 20 folders
	 deep (#11); comics with the same name show their format, e.g. "Normal (PDF)", long titles end with "..." and
	 the search finds words after the 24th character (#13)
	-GIF pages (#10)
	-Store: the chapter lists and searches of a store do not wait for its downloads (#8); "1 result", no "Load more"
	 after the last results, no Lua traceback in the messages, results without id are skipped (#14)
	-Messages centered on the window, the file name instead of the full path (#7)
	-Bugs fixed: tags lost for the comics named "[...]" (#1); memory leak of the first pages, 600 MB for a
	 library of 340 comics (#2); library disabled after a comic failed to open (#4); command line export: paths
	 longer than 260 characters, errors reported (#12)
	-Linux build again (CMake finds Lua and MuPDF as packaged by Debian/Ubuntu); GitHub Actions build of Linux and of
	 the Windows single exe, with a panel detection check on a generated comic (tests/make_test_comic.py)
ClaudeReader 1.0 (30/10/2026)
	-Windows: a single ClaudeReader.exe, no DLLs (every library linked statically: ./build.sh --static)
	-Library folders: the sub-folders of the library are shown as folder cards (categories), open one with a click,
	 back with Backspace or the path bar; the folder button of the toolbar switches to all the comics in one list
	-Tags: create, rename, recolor and delete them in the new Settings view (gear icon, Ctrl+,); right click a comic
	 to add or remove tags (or create one); tags shown on the cards, Tag filter in the toolbar, search matches
	 names and tags ("#name" searches the tags only). Tags follow the comic path in the library
	-Settings view: tags, library folder, open the library at start, store cache size and clearing
	-Store downloads named "<series> - <chapter>" (reading history and tags no longer shared between series)
	-Store: Cancel button while downloading (stops the current chapter, nothing written, empties the waiting list);
	 Mangapill home page shows the series names (was the chapter numbers "#48")
	-End of comic page in the reading area (no more dialog box): read the next comic of the folder,
	 restart, return to the library, open another comic; left arrow goes back to the last page
	-Large pages and long strips (webtoons): only the visible part is scaled (peak memory of an
	 800x60000 strip: 1.5 GB -> 250 MB) and the panels detection works on a reduced copy above 12 MP
	-WebP pages in archives and folders, page image extensions case insensitive
	-Store: browse, search and download comics and manga (activity bar bag icon, Ctrl+Shift+S).
	 Built-in stores MangaDex, Mangapill and Nyaa (torrents: magnet links for your torrent client);
	 stores are Lua scripts (Lua built in): add or fix stores in %APPDATA%\ClaudeReader\sources.
	 Downloads to the library as CBZ, PDF, ZIP or images, cached (pages, covers, searches), "Read" downloads
	 and opens a chapter. Command line: ClaudeReader --store list|<store> search|chapters|pages|download
	-Renamed ClaudeReader; settings, reading history and thumbnails moved from the BDReader folder automatically
	-VSCodium like dark theme: activity bar (Library, Reader, Open, Pages, Manga "JP" toggle, Fullscreen, Help),
	 side bar for the pages, flat status bar, dark title bar, Segoe UI, chevron navigation buttons, opaque panel frame
	-Library and reader views: switch with the activity bar or Ctrl+L, the open comic keeps its place
	-Library: dark cards with title and reading progress, explorer like path bar (folders, sub-folders menus,
	 editable path, folder chooser), sub-folders scanned recursively
	-Non-English file names (accents, Japanese...) open from the library, the Open dialog and "Open with"
	-Manga mode is a per comics setting (off by default)
	-Bugs fixed: random panel detection differences (out of bounds access in the original rectangles merging),
	 crash when maximizing (library resize), program path not terminated, overlapping sprintf
	-Manga mode with manga reading order (tiers top to bottom, right to left inside a tier, stacked
	 panels next to a tall one read top to bottom first), saved per comics: "Invert" checkbox in the status bar,
	 M shortcut or Navigation menu (navigation keys unchanged: right arrow = next panel); -r/--rtl for command line export (library sort "Invert" removed)
	-CMake build replacing autotools; Windows build with MSYS2 (UCRT64)
	-Ported to FLTK 1.4, OpenCV 4/5 and current MuPDF API; STLplus dependency removed
	-EPUB, XPS, FB2 and MOBI rendered with MuPDF; case insensitive file extensions
	-Windows: preferences and thumbnails stored in %APPDATA%\BDReader
	-Bugs fixed: crash on click while loading, library crash on unsupported files,
	 "show panel in context" not saved, command line export options ignored
Vincent Crocher 20/06/2016
v1.1
	-Comics library
	-New prefrences system
	-Magnifier (left click)
	-Quick zoom out (right click or spacebar)
	-Several bug fixed
v1.04
	-Border transparency when In Context
	-Pages rotation option (+90,-90,180)
	-Several bugs fixed (InContext switching bug, 'random' crashing, fallback to STRIP mode, global zoom preferences...)
	-Icon displayed in Windows version
	-PDF files now loaded at 300dpi
v1.031
	-Minimal (beta) support of Epub (3.0)
	-Update configure.ac for Mupdf detection
v1.03
	-New viewing/navgation: option to show panel in context, zoom options
	-Added a maximal zoom option to avoid to large zooming
	-Menus redesign
	-Display page number on fullscreen
	-Increase number of recent documents stored
	-Minimal command line options: help and version
	-Added CHANGES and README files in package
v1.02
   -Panel detection improved
   -Faster detection and navigation
   -Management of image folders: a folder of images (at least two) can now be open as a comic
   -Export function: any open comics can be exported as a series of images (one image per page or one image per panel): allow to use another reader while taking advantage of the panel detection, conversion from pdf to cbr...
   -Thumbnails view now displays previous and next pages (as well as current)
   -Navigation through the thumbnail view (mouse wheel: previous/next page and click on previous/next pages)
   -Strip/continuous navigation and view improved
   -Status bar clearly display reading mode
   -New (fancy !) Help window
   -Linux version: rename binary to bdreader (previously BDReader) to comply with GNU policy and creation of a man page
   -Some bug corrections
v1.01
   -Now open images archives (RAR, ZIP, TAR CB7 and 7Z files)
   -Strip mode view optimized to the window/screen size
   -Improvement of panels detection (can be slower on some comics)
   -Thumbnails bug correction
   -A few more navigation options (Go to page, first page, last page)
   -Better preferences management (window size and position, comic current page and individual view preferences for each document)
v0.99
   -Support for comics archives: CBR and CBZ files
v0.98
   -Package reorganization
   -Deb packaging
v0.97
   -Move to autotools instead of static Makefile to allow the classic: ./configure make make install
v0.95
   -Improvement of panels detection
   -Thumbnails of the current page
v0.9:
   -Improvement of Recent documents and folders management
   -Drag n' drop of files and "Open with" features added
   -Maximal zoom for panel view (avoid too important zooming on small panels)
   -Navigation buttons added
v0.8:
   First release